Derived from PySolFC
--------------------

The game logic is a translation into C of PySolFC's
(https://github.com/shlomif/PySolFC, read at commit 739f507, November
2026), which is licensed under the GNU GPL version 3 or later:

  - src/engine.c: the stacks' rules (acceptsCards, canMoveCards,
    canDropCards, canFlipCard, the talons' dealCards and canDealCards,
    the super move, autoPlay, isGameWon) from pysollib/stack.py and
    pysollib/game/__init__.py;
  - src/games.c: Klondike, Klondike by Threes, FreeCell, Spider (1, 2
    and 4 suits), Golf, Pyramid, Yukon and Russian Solitaire from
    pysollib/games/klondike.py, freecell.py, spider.py, golf.py,
    pyramid.py and yukon.py;
  - the deal numbers: Game.shuffle with LCRandom31 and ms_rearrange from
    pysol_cards (https://github.com/shlomif/pysol_cards, Expat licence,
    by Shlomi Fish), so a deal number gives PySolFC's deal of that number
    (its "ms" deals; plain numbers below 32000 are the same);
  - tools/pysol_ref.py: an independent transcription of the same deal
    code, used by the tests.

